  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to Ebola Epidemic in Sierra Leone through Social Mobilization in Bombali, Port Loko, Kamb</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD in partnership with the Catholic Diocese of Makeni (Caritas Makeni) is implementing a social mobilisation project in the Diocese of Makeni aimed at improving health and well being of vulnerable populations in Northern Sierra Leone. To stop the spread of the disease in the affected districts of Bombali, Port Loko, Kambia, Tonkolili and Koinadugu effective community-based social mobilisation on prevention measures is essential. Therefore the project strategy  includes; selection of 100 community advocate (CA) from the Catholic Parishes in the targeted area and train them for two day on prevention measure of EVD, 2) work closely with Ministry of Health and Sanitation, UNICEF, MSF and WHO to review and update current IEC material on Ebola, and 3) conducting 10 consecutive sensitizations during Sunday masses.</narrative>
  </description>
